.\" man/man3/Docv::Syntax.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Syntax" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Syntax \- Syntax highlighting of code blocks through tree\-sitter: a grammar (a shared library) and its \fB\%highlights.scm\fR query, both found where editors and tree\-sitter install them (nvim, helix, \fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/tree\-sitter\fR) or in docv\(aqs own data directory.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::Syntax\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Syntax highlighting of code blocks through tree\-sitter: a grammar (a
shared library) and its \fB\%highlights.scm\fR query, both found where editors
and tree\-sitter install them (nvim, helix, \fB\%$XDG_DATA_HOME/tree\-sitter\fR)
or in docv\(aqs own data directory. docv ships
neither; a language without both stays plain.
.PP
Captures map to \fB\%Markup\fR by their name, the longest known dotted prefix
first (\fB\%keyword.function\fR is a keyword). Within a code block an inner
capture overrides the one around it; of two captures of the same node
the later pattern wins (nvim\(aqs convention), or the earlier one for
queries of directories marked \fB\%first_wins\fR (helix\(aqs).
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
Docv::Syntax.highlight("x = 1 # one", "crystal") # => [[{"x", None}, ..., {"# one", SyntaxComment}]] or nil
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBALIASES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ALIASES = {
  "cr" => "crystal",
  "sh" => "bash",
  "shell" => "bash",
  "zsh" => "bash",
  "console" => "bash",
  "js" => "javascript",
  "mjs" => "javascript",
  "jsx" => "javascript",
  "ts" => "typescript",
  "py" => "python",
  "rb" => "ruby",
  "rs" => "rust",
  "yml" => "yaml",
  "md" => "markdown",
  "c++" => "cpp",
  "cxx" => "cpp",
  "hpp" => "cpp",
  "h" => "c",
  "cs" => "c_sharp",
  "csharp" => "c_sharp",
  "golang" => "go",
  "kt" => "kotlin",
  "ex" => "elixir",
  "exs" => "elixir",
  "hs" => "haskell",
  "ml" => "ocaml",
  "pl" => "perl",
  "ps1" => "powershell",
  "tf" => "hcl",
  "dockerfile" => "dockerfile",
  "html" => "html",
  "htm" => "html",
  "xml" => "xml",
  "scm" => "query",
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Code block labels (Markdown fence info) that name a grammar
differently; other labels are grammar names themselves.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBCAPTURES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
CAPTURES = {
  "keyword" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "conditional" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "repeat" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "include" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "exception" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "storageclass" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "define" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "preproc" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "label" => Markup::SyntaxKeyword,
  "string" => Markup::SyntaxString,
  "character" => Markup::SyntaxString,
  "comment" => Markup::SyntaxComment,
  "function" => Markup::SyntaxFunction,
  "method" => Markup::SyntaxFunction,
  "constructor" => Markup::SyntaxFunction,
  "type" => Markup::SyntaxType,
  "namespace" => Markup::SyntaxType,
  "module" => Markup::SyntaxType,
  "constant" => Markup::SyntaxConstant,
  "number" => Markup::SyntaxConstant,
  "float" => Markup::SyntaxConstant,
  "boolean" => Markup::SyntaxConstant,
  "variable.builtin" => Markup::SyntaxConstant,
  "operator" => Markup::SyntaxOperator,
  "punctuation" => Markup::SyntaxPunctuation,
  "property" => Markup::SyntaxProperty,
  "field" => Markup::SyntaxProperty,
  "attribute" => Markup::SyntaxProperty,
  "variable.member" => Markup::SyntaxProperty,
  "variable.other.member" => Markup::SyntaxProperty,
  "tag" => Markup::SyntaxTag,
  "variable" => Markup::None,
  "spell" => Markup::None,
  "nospell" => Markup::None,
  "none" => Markup::None,
  "conceal" => Markup::None,
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Capture names (and their dotted prefixes) and what they mark. \fB\%None\fR
marks a name as plain; names not listed are ignored, as are names
starting with \fB\%_\fR.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBINHERITS = /\eA;+\es*inherits\es*:?\es*(.+)/\fR
A query line naming the languages whose queries come first:
\fB\%; \%inherits: \%ecma,jsx\fR (nvim; a name in parentheses is optional).
.TP 4
\fBQUERY_FILE = "highlights.scm"\fR
The query file of a language in a query directory.
.TP 4
\fBSECTION_LANGUAGES = {"cr" => "crystal"}\fR
Languages of the code examples of manual pages by the letters after
their section number: \fB\%docv \%gen\-cr\fR writes \fB\%Foo.3cr\fR.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.apply(blocks : Array(Block), language : String) : Nil\fR
Highlights the consecutive \fIblocks\fR of one code example as \fIlanguage\fR:
each text block a line, each blank block that many empty lines. Spans
of marked text keep their block\(aqs style with the markup set.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.clear : Nil\fR
Forgets the loaded grammars, so changed directories take effect.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.grammar_directories : Array(String)\fR
Grammar directories searched after \fB\%TreeSitter::Language.directories\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.grammar_directories=(grammar_directories : Array(String))\fR
Grammar directories searched after \fB\%TreeSitter::Language.directories\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.highlight(code : String, language : String) : Array(Array(Tuple(String, Markup))) | Nil\fR
The lines of \fIcode\fR as runs of text with their markup; \fB\%nil\fR when
\fIlanguage\fR has no grammar or no highlight query (or they do not fit).
.TP 4
\fBdef self.language(label : String) : String | Nil\fR
The grammar name of a code block \fIlabel\fR (\fB\%ALIASES\fR, lower case, first
word of a fence info string); \fB\%nil\fR for an empty label.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.markup(name : String) : Markup | Nil\fR
The markup of capture \fIname\fR: the longest of its dotted prefixes in
\fB\%CAPTURES\fR; \fB\%nil\fR for plain and unknown names.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.page_language(path : String | Nil) : String | Nil\fR
The language of the code examples of the manual page at \fIpath\fR
(\fB\%SECTION_LANGUAGES\fR), if any.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.query_directories : Array(QueryDirectory)\fR
Query directories, searched in order for \fB\%<language>/highlights.scm\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.query_directories=(query_directories : Array(QueryDirectory))\fR
Query directories, searched in order for \fB\%<language>/highlights.scm\fR.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/syntax.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
